quran[7]{c,v,t}:
  9,55,"Nothing prevents their charities from being accepted, except that they disbelieve in Allah and His Messenger (blessings and peace be upon him), and do not perform prayer but lazily (and unwillingly). And they do not spend (in charity) but reluctantly."
  9,56,"So let not their wealth nor their children impress you. Allah only wants to punish them through these things in this worldly life, and their souls will depart while they are disbelievers."
  9,57,"(O believers!) They swear by Allah that they are part of you, but they are not part of you. Instead, they are cowardly people."
  9,58,"If they could find a refuge, or a cave, or a hole to enter (into the earth), they would turn towards it with great haste."
  9,59,"Some of them blame you regarding (the distribution of) charitable offerings. If they are given some of it, they are pleased, but if they are not given some of it, they are enraged."
  9,60,"(It would have been better) if they had been pleased with what Allah and His Messenger (blessings and peace be upon him) gave them, and had said: ‘Allah is sufficient for us; Allah will give us out of His grace, and so will His Messenger (blessings and peace be upon him). Indeed, to Allah we turn in hope.’"
  9,61,"The prescribed charities (i.e. zakat) are only for the poor, the needy, the officials employed to collect them, and those whose hearts are (to be) reconciled, and for (the freedom of) the captives, and for the debtors, and (those) in the way of Allah and for the travellers. (This is) an obligation from Allah, and Allah is All-Knowing, All-Wise."
